|errata_history=This is the errata version PC-E1 of [[Kashyyyk: Sacred Falls (Forest)]] (version 2 of 2). The image here is the current Players Committee card image published 1 June 2022. This is the current text. Each version below is quoted in full with its dated source.
* '''Original''' ([[Kashyyyk: Sacred Falls (Forest)]]): Virtual Set 16 release; card image first published 3 September 2021<ref name="img-o-0">Players Committee card image <code>Virtual16-Light/large/kashyyyksacredfallsforest.gif</code> as published 3 September 2021: [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/blob/b4a011ace2799d9e188578c4043193ff94a7a06c/Images-HT/starwars/Virtual16-Light/large/kashyyyksacredfallsforest.gif holotable commit b4a011a] (the PC's card-image repository, which serves res.starwarsccg.org/cards).</ref>: “Light: Your Wookiees move from here for free when using landspeed. Dark: While opponent occupies with a Wookiee, your Force generation here is canceled.”
* '''PC-E1''' (this page): Card image published 1 June 2022, and the current [https://res.starwarsccg.org/cardlists/Set16Type.html Virtual Set 16 card list]<ref name="img-PC-E1-0">Players Committee card image <code>Virtual16-Light/large/kashyyyksacredfallsforest.gif</code> as published 1 June 2022: [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/blob/e8445f08fa931119eec2c3f95d5cea095145da26/Images-HT/starwars/Virtual16-Light/large/kashyyyksacredfallsforest.gif holotable commit e8445f0] (the PC's card-image repository, which serves res.starwarsccg.org/cards).</ref>: “Light: Your Wookiees move from here for free when using landspeed. Dark: While opponent occupies with a Wookiee, your Force generation here is canceled.” '''What changed:''' No change to the game text words. Visible changes on the image only: the PC re-rendered the Virtual Set 16 card images (the side credit and copyright lines and the typesetting of the game text changed; on some cards icons or the set-icon position also changed); the game text words are the same. A version under Bill's 12 November 2026 ruling (every visible change on a PC image is a version).
